AI Documentation for HW3

Tool used:
ChatGPT Codex (GPT-5)

My work and use of AI:
This package builds on my own HW2 project, including the Tennis Abstract data
source, the original Serena Williams data-cleaning workflow, and the plotting
goal. I used ChatGPT Codex primarily as a coding reviewer and debugging
assistant while converting that existing work into a reusable R package.

Main types of prompts:
- I shared my HW2 code and asked for help identifying changes needed to turn
  the workflow into package functions.
- I asked for targeted help debugging errors I encountered while retrieving,
  parsing, and cleaning Tennis Abstract data.
- I asked for suggestions about handling the different ATP and WTA file
  formats, organizing small helper functions, and writing local tests.
- I asked for feedback on whether the final package satisfied the HW3
  requirements.

How I used the suggestions:
- I decided which functions, inputs, outputs, and package structure to use.
- I adapted my prior HW2 workflow and integrated revisions into the files in
  R/ myself.
- I used debugging suggestions to resolve JavaScript parsing and player
  birth-date retrieval issues.
- I used feedback to revise tests in tests/testthat/, improve README.md, and
  check Git and installation steps.

Verification and responsibility:
I ran the code myself throughout development, inspected the returned data
frames and plots, and tested the package with both Rafael Nadal and Serena
Williams. I ran the local offline test suite and verified installation from
GitHub. I reviewed the final code, made the final decisions about what to
include, and can explain the purpose and behavior of each submitted function.